  partName: Sensor (6)
  description: The Sensor (6) is a tiny, complex device positioned at the top-right-rear
    of the engine, constructed from Material.001, responsible for monitoring and
    reporting critical engine parameters, such as temperature and pressure, which
    is vital for optimal engine performance and efficiency. Its complex shape allows
    for precise measurements and its rear position enables it to capture data from
    the engine's exhaust system. Notably, the Sensor (6) is calibrated to provide
    accurate readings even in extreme operating conditions.
